We are given the following information:

- John has **20 minutes of math homework**.
- John has **40 minutes of reading homework**.
- John has **20 minutes of history homework**.
- He has **3 hours** before he has to eat dinner.

We are to find **how many minutes John has to nap**.

---

### Step 1: Convert all time to **minutes**

- 3 hours = 3 × 60 = **180 minutes**

---

### Step 2: Add up the total time spent on homework

$$
20 \text{ (math)} + 40 \text{ (reading)} + 20 \text{ (history)} = 80 \text{ minutes}
$$

---

### Step 3: Subtract the homework time from the total time before dinner

$$
180 \text{ minutes (before dinner)} - 80 \text{ minutes (homework)} = \quad \text{?}
$$

$$
180 - 80 = \quad \text{100 minutes}
$$

---

